<title>FRANCE: LVMH has no comment on report of DFS talks.</title>
<headline>LVMH has no comment on report of DFS talks.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French luxury goods group LVMH declined comment on a report in the Wall Street Journal that it was close to reaching an agreement to buy the remaining shares in U.S. duty free chain DFS that it does not own.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no comment on the Wall Street Journal report,&quot; a spokeswoman for LVMH said.</p>
<p>The Journal said LVMH was in advanced talks with the lone holdout partner at DFS, Robert Miller, about buying his 38.75 percent stake and a deal could be struck in a matter of weeks. LVMH has bought 61.25 percent of DFS for around $2.6 billion.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
